{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:23:18Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 57, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "185\t  Escape has no native form behavior:\n186\t  `if (e.key === 'Escape') cancelEdit()`.\n187\t- **Tab order**: Save then Cancel, matching DOM/visual order left-to-right \u2014\n188\t  no `tabIndex` overrides needed.\n189\t- **Focus ring**: rely on the browser default (project sets no `outline:\n190\t  none` anywhere today) \u2014 `focus-states` is satisfied for free.\n191\t- **Touch targets**: Save/Cancel/Edit reuse the existing `button` rule\n192\t  unchanged (`padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem`), same as Done/Delete today. That\n193\t  rule's rendered height is under the 44\u00d744 recommendation project-wide \u2014\n194\t  true for every button in this app already, not something this feature\n195\t  introduces or is scoped to fix (non-goal territory: this cycle extends\n196\t  `.task`, it doesn't redesign the button system). Flagging it here so it's\n197\t  a known, pre-existing characteristic rather than a silent gap.\n198\t- **Row gap**: existing `.task` `gap: 0.5rem` (8px) already satisfies\n199\t  `touch-spacing` between the new buttons \u2014 no change needed.\n200\t- Input `aria-label=\"Task title\"` \u2014 reuses `AddTask.jsx`'s exact label\n201\t  (line 20). Fine to reuse verbatim: only one row is ever in edit mode at a\n202\t  time (assumption 2), so there's never a duplicate-label ambiguity for\n203\t  screen readers at any given moment.\n204\t- `Edit`/`Save`/`Cancel` buttons get `aria-label`s that include the task\n205\t  title, matching the existing `Complete ${task.title}` / `Delete\n206\t  ${task.title}` convention:\n207\t  - `aria-label={`Edit ${task.title}`}`\n208\t  - `aria-label={`Save new title for ${task.title}`}`\n209\t  - `aria-label={`Cancel editing ${task.title}`}`\n210\t\n211\t## Exact code changes\n212\t\n213\t**`frontend/src/api.js`** \u2014 add next to `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (after\n214\tline 21):", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XXa5WFrmhPR2wMdKayKsVH", "session_id": "58fceeb3-b436-44c4-aa8c-c256d25c46e2"}}
