{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:25:11Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 141, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Implementation: Edit a task title\n2\t\n3\tTaiga #2 \u00b7 implements `docs/spec.md` + `docs/design.md`\n4\t\n5\t## What changed, by file\n6\t\n7\t- **`backend/app/store.py`** \u2014 `TaskStore.set_title(task_id, title)`: looks up\n8\t  the task, returns `None` if missing (mirrors `set_done`'s existing\n9\t  not-found pattern), else sets `.title` and returns the task.\n10\t- **`backend/app/main.py`** \u2014 `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}`, reusing the\n11\t  existing `TaskIn` model so an empty/oversized title 422s before the\n12\t  handler runs. 404s via `HTTPException` if `set_title` returns `None`.\n13\t- **`frontend/src/api.js`** \u2014 `updateTask(id, title)`, same `request()`\n14\t  wrapper as the other calls.\n15\t- **`frontend/src/App.jsx`** \u2014 wires `onEdit` through the existing `run()`\n16\t  error-handling wrapper, same shape as `onComplete`/`onDelete`.\n17\t- **`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`** \u2014 per-row edit mode: `Edit`\n18\t  button (between `Done` and `Delete`) swaps the row's title span + actions\n19\t  for a `<form>` with an autofocused input and Save/Cancel buttons. Client-side\n20\t  trim-check blocks empty saves before any request, mirroring `AddTask.jsx`.\n21\t  `Escape` and `Cancel` both revert with no request sent. Only one row can be\n22\t  in edit mode at a time (starting a new edit discards any unsaved draft).\n23\t- **`frontend/src/App.css`** \u2014 styles for the edit form/input/error message,\n24\t  reusing existing color tokens only.\n25\t- **`backend/tests/test_tasks.py`** \u2014 success/404/422 cases for `PATCH`.\n26\t- **`e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`** \u2014 real-browser coverage for AC1-5 and both\n27\t  open-question defaults (done tasks stay editable; single-task edit mode).\n28\t\n29\t## Fix-cycle addendum (attempt 2)\n30\t\n31\tThe test stage found a real defect via a live browser test: the edit\n32\tinput and the always-present `AddTask` input both had\n33\t`aria-label=\"Task title\"`, so as soon as any row entered edit mode two\n34\tinputs shared one accessible name. `docs/design.md`'s reasoning about\n35\t`aria-label` collisions only considered row-vs-row, not row-vs-AddTask.\n36\t\n37\tRoot-cause fix: `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`'s edit input now\n38\tuses `aria-label={\\`Edit title for ${task.title}\\`}` \u2014 same per-row-title\n39\tpattern already used by the Save/Cancel/Complete/Edit/Delete buttons next to\n40\tit, so it's both unique and consistent with the rest of the row.\n41\t\n42\tUpdated `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`:\n43\t- `edit_input()` now locates by `Edit title for {title}` instead of the\n44\t  ambiguous shared label (still scoped to `ul.task-list` as a second layer\n45\t  of disambiguation).\n46\t- The test that documented the collision as a known defect\n47\t  (`test_edit_input_shares_the_add_tasks_accessible_name`) is now\n48\t  `test_edit_input_has_a_distinct_accessible_name`, asserting `\"Task title\"`\n49\t  resolves to exactly one element (AddTask's) and `\"Edit title for buy milk\"`\n50\t  resolves to exactly one element (the edit input) while a row is in edit mode.\n51\t\n52\tVerified in this session:\n53\t- `python3 -m pytest backend/tests e2e/ -q` \u2192 42/42 pass\n54\t- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 clean\n55\t\n56\t## Known limitations / follow-ups (unchanged from review, not addressed here)\n57\t\n58\t- `frontend/src/api.js`'s `request()` renders FastAPI's 422 `detail` (a list\n59\t  of validation-error objects) as `\"[object Object]\"` in the error banner for\n60\t  the oversized-title case (AC5). Pre-existing, shared with `AddTask`'s\n61\t  create path, out of scope per `docs/design.md:64-71`.\n62\t- No frontend unit-test framework is installed (`frontend/package.json` has\n63\t  no `test` script despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test`); AC1-5\n64\t  coverage lives in the Playwright e2e suite instead.\n65\t- `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` is a leftover untracked scratch file\n66\t  from the test stage's manual 422-shape inspection. It is **not** part of\n67\t  this implementation and should be deleted before commit; this session's\n68\t  sandbox permissions block `rm`/`git clean` on it (same restriction the\n69\t  test stage hit), so it's still present in the working tree.\n70\t\n71\t## How to verify\n72\t\n73\t```bash\n74\tcd backend  && python3 -m pytest -q\n75\tpython3 -m pytest backend/tests e2e/ -q   # from repo root, real Chromium e2e\n76\tcd frontend && npm run build\n77\t```\n78\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01J5MPWkZeTxwEPExAmfdaLF", "session_id": "58fceeb3-b436-44c4-aa8c-c256d25c46e2"}}
